Feature: Validation of Data Consistency Between product_plant and product_plant_v2 Tables

  The Databricks PySpark script compares each column value from product_plant and product_plant_v2 tables using plant_id as the join key. For each column, a validation column is generated indicating "Match" or "Mismatch". The results are stored in the pp_validation_results table, with columns ordered as: source column, target column, validation column for each attribute. The script must handle missing rows, nulls, and data type mismatches, and log errors in the error_message column.

  Background:
    Given the source table "purgo_playground.product_plant" exists with defined schema
    And the target table "purgo_playground.product_plant_v2" exists with defined schema
    And the output table "purgo_playground.pp_validation_results" is dropped and recreated with the required schema
    And all columns from both tables are aliased as _src and _tgt respectively in the output
    And plant_id is used as the join/comparison key
    And all validation columns are of type string and contain either "Match", "Mismatch", or a specific error message
    And missing rows in either source or target are flagged in missing_from_src or missing_from_tgt columns
    And any data type conversion errors or null handling issues are logged in error_message column

  Scenario Outline: Validate matching rows between product_plant and product_plant_v2
    Given a row exists in product_plant with plant_id = <plant_id> and the following values:
      | plant_cd         | company_cd      | source_system_cd | product_line     | primary_uom_cd | global_uom_conversion_rate | global_uom_cd | lifecycle_status | flais_active | sales_rank_abc | inventory_rank_abc | make_buy |
      | <plant_cd_src>   | <company_cd_src>| <source_system_cd_src> | <product_line_src> | <primary_uom_cd_src> | <global_uom_conversion_rate_src> | <global_uom_cd_src> | <lifecycle_status_src> | <flais_active_src> | <sales_rank_abc_src> | <inventory_rank_abc_src> | <make_buy_src> |
    And a row exists in product_plant_v2 with plant_id = <plant_id> and the following values:
      | plant_cd         | company_cd      | source_system_cd | product_line     | primary_uom_cd | global_uom_conversion_rate | global_uom_cd | lifecycle_status | flais_active | sales_rank_abc | inventory_rank_abc | make_buy |
      | <plant_cd_tgt>   | <company_cd_tgt>| <source_system_cd_tgt> | <product_line_tgt> | <primary_uom_cd_tgt> | <global_uom_conversion_rate_tgt> | <global_uom_cd_tgt> | <lifecycle_status_tgt> | <flais_active_tgt> | <sales_rank_abc_tgt> | <inventory_rank_abc_tgt> | <make_buy_tgt> |
    When the script compares each column value between product_plant and product_plant_v2 for plant_id = <plant_id>
    Then the pp_validation_results table contains a row with:
      | plant_id_src | plant_id_tgt | plant_id_validation |
      | <plant_id>   | <plant_id>   | <plant_id_validation> |
    And for each column, the validation column is set to "Match" if values are equal (including null=null), otherwise "Mismatch"
    And missing_from_src and missing_from_tgt are null
    And error_message is null

    Examples:
      | plant_id | plant_cd_src | plant_cd_tgt | plant_id_validation | company_cd_src | company_cd_tgt | company_cd_validation | source_system_cd_src | source_system_cd_tgt | source_system_cd_validation | product_line_src | product_line_tgt | product_line_validation | primary_uom_cd_src | primary_uom_cd_tgt | primary_uom_cd_validation | global_uom_conversion_rate_src | global_uom_conversion_rate_tgt | global_uom_conversion_rate_validation | global_uom_cd_src | global_uom_cd_tgt | global_uom_cd_validation | lifecycle_status_src | lifecycle_status_tgt | lifecycle_status_validation | flais_active_src | flais_active_tgt | flais_active_validation | sales_rank_abc_src | sales_rank_abc_tgt | sales_rank_abc_validation | inventory_rank_abc_src | inventory_rank_abc_tgt | inventory_rank_abc_validation | make_buy_src | make_buy_tgt | make_buy_validation |
      | 101      | PLANT_A      | PLANT_A      | Match              | CO1           | CO1           | Match                | SYS1               | SYS1               | Match                      | PRODLINE1        | PRODLINE1        | Match                  | UOM1              | UOM1              | Match                    | 1.0                        | 1.0                        | Match                              | GUOM1           | GUOM1           | Match                  | ACTIVE             | ACTIVE             | Match                  | Y               | Y               | Match                  | A                 | A                 | Match                  | B                   | B                   | Match                      | MAKE         | MAKE         | Match              |
      | 102      | PLANT_B      | PLANT_C      | Mismatch           | CO2           | CO2           | Match                | SYS2               | SYS2               | Match                      | PRODLINE2        | PRODLINE2        | Match                  | UOM2              | UOM2              | Match                    | 2.5                        | 2.5                        | Match                              | GUOM2           | GUOM2           | Match                  | INACTIVE           | ACTIVE             | Mismatch               | N               | Y               | Mismatch               | B                 | C                 | Mismatch               | C                   | C                   | Match                      | BUY          | MAKE         | Mismatch           |

  Scenario Outline: Handle missing rows in product_plant (source)
    Given a row exists in product_plant_v2 with plant_id = <plant_id> and the following values:
      | plant_cd         | company_cd      | source_system_cd | product_line     | primary_uom_cd | global_uom_conversion_rate | global_uom_cd | lifecycle_status | flais_active | sales_rank_abc | inventory_rank_abc | make_buy |
      | <plant_cd_tgt>   | <company_cd_tgt>| <source_system_cd_tgt> | <product_line_tgt> | <primary_uom_cd_tgt> | <global_uom_conversion_rate_tgt> | <global_uom_cd_tgt> | <lifecycle_status_tgt> | <flais_active_tgt> | <sales_rank_abc_tgt> | <inventory_rank_abc_tgt> | <make_buy_tgt> |
    And no row exists in product_plant with plant_id = <plant_id>
    When the script compares rows for plant_id = <plant_id>
    Then the pp_validation_results table contains a row with:
      | plant_id_src | plant_id_tgt | plant_id_validation |
      | null         | <plant_id>   | Mismatch            |
    And all *_src columns are null
    And all *_tgt columns are populated from product_plant_v2
    And all *_validation columns are set to "Mismatch"
    And missing_from_src is set to "Missing in Source"
    And missing_from_tgt is null
    And error_message is null

    Examples:
      | plant_id | plant_cd_tgt | company_cd_tgt | source_system_cd_tgt | product_line_tgt | primary_uom_cd_tgt | global_uom_conversion_rate_tgt | global_uom_cd_tgt | lifecycle_status_tgt | flais_active_tgt | sales_rank_abc_tgt | inventory_rank_abc_tgt | make_buy_tgt |
      | 201      | PLANT_X      | COX           | SYSX               | PRODLINEX        | UOMX              | 3.0                        | GUOMX           | ACTIVE             | Y               | X                 | X                   | MAKE         |

  Scenario Outline: Handle missing rows in product_plant_v2 (target)
    Given a row exists in product_plant with plant_id = <plant_id> and the following values:
      | plant_cd         | company_cd      | source_system_cd | product_line     | primary_uom_cd | global_uom_conversion_rate | global_uom_cd | lifecycle_status | flais_active | sales_rank_abc | inventory_rank_abc | make_buy |
      | <plant_cd_src>   | <company_cd_src>| <source_system_cd_src> | <product_line_src> | <primary_uom_cd_src> | <global_uom_conversion_rate_src> | <global_uom_cd_src> | <lifecycle_status_src> | <flais_active_src> | <sales_rank_abc_src> | <inventory_rank_abc_src> | <make_buy_src> |
    And no row exists in product_plant_v2 with plant_id = <plant_id>
    When the script compares rows for plant_id = <plant_id>
    Then the pp_validation_results table contains a row with:
      | plant_id_src | plant_id_tgt | plant_id_validation |
      | <plant_id>   | null         | Mismatch            |
    And all *_src columns are populated from product_plant
    And all *_tgt columns are null
    And all *_validation columns are set to "Mismatch"
    And missing_from_src is null
    And missing_from_tgt is set to "Missing in Target"
    And error_message is null

    Examples:
      | plant_id | plant_cd_src | company_cd_src | source_system_cd_src | product_line_src | primary_uom_cd_src | global_uom_conversion_rate_src | global_uom_cd_src | lifecycle_status_src | flais_active_src | sales_rank_abc_src | inventory_rank_abc_src | make_buy_src |
      | 202      | PLANT_Y      | COY           | SYSY               | PRODLINEY        | UOMY              | 4.5                        | GUOMY           | INACTIVE           | N               | Y                 | Z                   | BUY          |

  Scenario Outline: Handle null values in columns
    Given a row exists in product_plant with plant_id = <plant_id> and the following values:
      | plant_cd         | company_cd      | source_system_cd | product_line     | primary_uom_cd | global_uom_conversion_rate | global_uom_cd | lifecycle_status | flais_active | sales_rank_abc | inventory_rank_abc | make_buy |
      | <plant_cd_src>   | <company_cd_src>| <source_system_cd_src> | <product_line_src> | <primary_uom_cd_src> | <global_uom_conversion_rate_src> | <global_uom_cd_src> | <lifecycle_status_src> | <flais_active_src> | <sales_rank_abc_src> | <inventory_rank_abc_src> | <make_buy_src> |
    And a row exists in product_plant_v2 with plant_id = <plant_id> and the following values:
      | plant_cd         | company_cd      | source_system_cd | product_line     | primary_uom_cd | global_uom_conversion_rate | global_uom_cd | lifecycle_status | flais_active | sales_rank_abc | inventory_rank_abc | make_buy |
      | <plant_cd_tgt>   | <company_cd_tgt>| <source_system_cd_tgt> | <product_line_tgt> | <primary_uom_cd_tgt> | <global_uom_conversion_rate_tgt> | <global_uom_cd_tgt> | <lifecycle_status_tgt> | <flais_active_tgt> | <sales_rank_abc_tgt> | <inventory_rank_abc_tgt> | <make_buy_tgt> |
    When the script compares each column value between product_plant and product_plant_v2 for plant_id = <plant_id>
    Then for each column, if both values are null, the validation column is set to "Match"
    And if one value is null and the other is not, the validation column is set to "Mismatch"
    And error_message is null

    Examples:
      | plant_id | plant_cd_src | plant_cd_tgt | plant_cd_validation | company_cd_src | company_cd_tgt | company_cd_validation |
      | 301      | null         | null         | Match              | CO3           | null           | Mismatch              |
      | 302      | PLANT_Z      | null         | Mismatch           | null          | CO4            | Mismatch              |

  Scenario Outline: Handle data type mismatches or conversion errors
    Given a row exists in product_plant with plant_id = <plant_id> and the following values:
      | global_uom_conversion_rate |
      | <global_uom_conversion_rate_src> |
    And a row exists in product_plant_v2 with plant_id = <plant_id> and the following values:
      | global_uom_conversion_rate |
      | <global_uom_conversion_rate_tgt> |
    When the script attempts to compare global_uom_conversion_rate between product_plant and product_plant_v2 for plant_id = <plant_id>
    Then if a data type conversion error occurs, the global_uom_conversion_rate_validation column is set to "Error"
    And error_message contains "Data type mismatch for global_uom_conversion_rate"
    And other validation columns are processed as per normal rules

    Examples:
      | plant_id | global_uom_conversion_rate_src | global_uom_conversion_rate_tgt |
      | 401      | "not_a_number"                | 5.0                           |
      | 402      | 6.0                           | "NaN"                         |

  Scenario: Logging errors for unexpected exceptions during validation
    Given an unexpected exception occurs during the validation process for plant_id = 501
    When the script processes the row
    Then the error_message column in pp_validation_results contains the exception details
    And all validation columns for the row are set to "Error"
    And missing_from_src and missing_from_tgt are null

  Scenario: Column order in pp_validation_results table
    Given the pp_validation_results table is created
    Then the columns are ordered as: source column, target column, validation column for each attribute, in the following sequence:
      | plant_id_src | plant_id_tgt | plant_id_validation |
      | plant_cd_src | plant_cd_tgt | plant_cd_validation |
      | company_cd_src | company_cd_tgt | company_cd_validation |
      | source_system_cd_src | source_system_cd_tgt | source_system_cd_validation |
      | product_line_src | product_line_tgt | product_line_validation |
      | primary_uom_cd_src | primary_uom_cd_tgt | primary_uom_cd_validation |
      | global_uom_conversion_rate_src | global_uom_conversion_rate_tgt | global_uom_conversion_rate_validation |
      | global_uom_cd_src | global_uom_cd_tgt | global_uom_cd_validation |
      | lifecycle_status_src | lifecycle_status_tgt | lifecycle_status_validation |
      | flais_active_src | flais_active_tgt | flais_active_validation |
      | sales_rank_abc_src | sales_rank_abc_tgt | sales_rank_abc_validation |
      | inventory_rank_abc_src | inventory_rank_abc_tgt | inventory_rank_abc_validation |
      | make_buy_src | make_buy_tgt | make_buy_validation |
      | missing_from_src | missing_from_tgt | error_message |

  Scenario: Validation script execution frequency and volume
    Given the script is scheduled to run daily on all rows in product_plant and product_plant_v2
    And the expected volume is up to 10 million rows per table
    Then the script must process all rows efficiently and populate pp_validation_results accordingly

  Scenario: Audit trail and logging requirements
    Given the validation process is executed
    Then any row-level errors, mismatches, or exceptions are logged in the error_message column of pp_validation_results
    And a summary of validation statistics (counts of matches, mismatches, errors) is logged in purgo_playground.d_product_plant_processed_error_log with timestamp and details

